  "summary": "The Mexican government presented a study on how the tariffs affect its auto industry.",
  "lead": {
    "h1": "Mexico asks the US to pause steel and auto tariffs during the trade-agreement review",
    "context": "The Mexican government presented a study on how the tariffs affect its auto industry.",
    "background": "US and Mexican officials have discussed steel, aluminum and automobiles in three review rounds. They scheduled a fourth bilateral round for September.",
    "view": "Mexico has made tariff relief a negotiating request, not a concession it has won. The practical result depends on whether Washington accepts a pause or offers a narrower reduction.",
    "prediction": "The September round is the next stated test. Tariff relief in the joint statement would confirm movement. Another statement limited to continued talks would weaken that view.",
